  "findings": [
    "Direct Tier 3 and Tier 4 each retain six of eight authored positive correspondences; the lights and migration paraphrases fall below the fixed cosine threshold.",
    "All six declared other-origin controls produce direct semantic candidates, including equivalent text, identical text and whole-statement negation. This limits origin specificity; it does not automatically mean the similarity score is wrong.",
    "All sixteen ordinary cascade comparisons exit at Tier 2. No ordered Tier 3 or Tier 4 invocation is observed on this fixture matrix.",
    "Both ambiguous references remain unknown. No skipped or incomplete semantic stage was counted as a negative prediction."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Authored positive correspondence is a semantic design judgment, while negative origin is established by a declared copy program; these are distinct reference contracts.",
    "The deliberately identical other-origin control is unidentifiable from text alone. A matcher cannot recover an origin choice that the observed text does not encode.",
    "The two positive misses are component diagnostic examples, not proof of a general reproduction gap or broad semantic failure.",
    "A direct semantic component result is not evidence that the live ordinary cascade used that component.",
    "Population attribution accuracy, adversarial attack success, malicious influence, hidden reliance and defense benefit are not measured here.",
    "Multiple measurements of the same sixteen fixtures are correlated diagnostics; no p-values, population confidence intervals or independent-sample claims are supported."
  ],
